        {"old": "    string Tmp, DateTimeOffset Now, TimeSpan MinAge, Func<long, Probe> Probe, Func<string, bool>? Mine = null, SweepHooks? Hooks = null);", "new": "    string Tmp, DateTimeOffset Now, TimeSpan MinAge, Func<long, Probe> Probe, Func<string, bool>? Mine = null, SweepHooks? Hooks = null, TimeSpan? SweepLockWait = null);", "count": 1, "reason": "entry 5.1 (consult e9d7aec0; F29 of the conventions' follow-ups plan): SweepOptions gains the wait of the Windows sweep lock, a test seam (default 30 s). Directory.Move has no single winner on Windows \u2014 two threads racing one source both succeed in 39951 of 40000 races (hosted windows-latest, run 41873954643) \u2014 so two sweeps at once can double-report and restore a folder unclaimed."},
        {"old": "        var pass = new Pass(options);\n        try\n        {\n            pass.Go();\n        }\n        catch (Exception ex)\n        {\n            pass.Fail(\"sweep\", ex);\n        }\n\n        return pass.Result();", "new": "        var pass = new Pass(options);\n        using var lease = SweepLock.Take(options.Tmp, options.SweepLockWait, pass.Note); // Windows: one sweep at a time over a root (E5 entry 5.1); POSIX: holds nothing\n        if (!lease.Granted) return pass.Result();\n        try\n        {\n            pass.Go();\n        }\n        catch (Exception ex)\n        {\n            pass.Fail(\"sweep\", ex);\n        }\n\n        return pass.Result();", "count": 1, "reason": "entry 5.1 (consult e9d7aec0; F29): on Windows the whole pass runs under a named mutex over the root (SweepLock.cs, coai's own file), because Directory.Move has no single winner there; a sweep that cannot take it lists one line and sweeps nothing."},
        {"old": "        public void Fail(string label, Exception ex) => _errors.Add($\"{label}: {FirstLine(ex)}\");", "new": "        public void Fail(string label, Exception ex) => _errors.Add($\"{label}: {FirstLine(ex)}\");\n\n        public void Note(string line) => _listed.Add(line);", "count": 1, "reason": "entry 5.1 (consult e9d7aec0; F29): on Windows the whole pass runs under a named mutex over the root (SweepLock.cs, coai's own file), because Directory.Move has no single winner there; a sweep that cannot take it lists one line and sweeps nothing. (the line is listed through Pass.Note)"}
    ] },
